912: 
913:        Abbreviations
914:        The following abbreviations apply to binary multiples and register access:
915: 
916:        � Binary multiples
917: 
918:             The abbreviations K, M, and G (kilo, mega, and giga) represent binary
919:             multiples and have the following values:
920: 
921:        K = 210 (1024)
922:        M = 220 (1,048,576)
923:        G = 230 (1,073,741,824)
924: 
925:        For example:  2 kilobytes =  2 2 210 bytes
926:                      4 megabytes =  2 4 220 bytes
927:        2 KB =        8 gigabytes =  2 8 230 bytes
928:        4 MB =
929:        8 GB =
930: 
931: xviii
932: � Register Access
933:      The abbreviations used to indicate the type of access to register fields and
934:      bits have the following definitions:
935:           IGN -- Ignore
936:           Bits and fields specified as IGN are ignored when written.
937: 
938:           MBZ -- Must Be Zero
939:           Software must never place a nonzero value in bits and fields specified
940:           as MBZ. Such fields are reserved for future use. An illegal operand
941:           exception occurs if the processor encounters a nonzero value in a field
942:           specified as MBZ.
943: 
944:           RAX -- Read As UNDEFINED
945:           Bits and fields specified as RAX are unimplemented bits of registers
946:           that read as UNDEFINED.1
947: 
948:           RAZ -- Read As Zero
949:           Bits and fields specified as RAZ return a zero when read.
950: 
951:           RC -- Read Clears
952:           Bits and fields specified as RC are cleared when read. Unless otherwise
953:           specified, such fields cannot be written.1
954: 
955:           RES -- Reserved
956:           Bits and fields specified as RES are reserved by Digital and should not
957:           be used.1
958: 
959:           RO -- Read Only
960:           Bits and fields specified as RO can be read and are ignored (not written)
961:           on write operations.1
962: 
963:           RW -- Read and Write
964:           Bits and fields specified as RW can be read and written. Writing a zero
965:           clears the bits.1
966: 
967: 1 Implementation-specific or typographical convention adapted from or not specified in
968:     the Alpha Architecture Reference Manual.
969: 
970:                                                                                                                          xix
971:     R/W1C -- Read and Write One to Clear
972: 
973:     Bits and fields specified as R/W1C can be read. Writing a one clears
974:     the bits.1
975: 
976:     WA -- Write Always Clears
977:     Bits and fields specified as WA can be read. Any write clears the bits.
978: 
979:     WO -- Write Only
980: 
981:     Bits and fields specified as WO can be written but not read. In the I/O
982:     controller the results of reading such registers are UNPREDICTABLE.
983:     Writing a zero clears the bits.1
984: 
985:     X
986: 
987:     Bits and fields specified as X return UNPREDICTABLE results when
988:     read and are ignored on write operations.1
989: 
