10256: 6.4.3 Status 0 Register
10257: 
10258:             The IOC logs error information in the status 0 (IOC_STAT0) register as follows:
10259: 
10260:             � If the ERR bit (<4>) is not set when an IOC error is detected, all of the
10261:                   register bits are updated and the ERR bit is set.
10262: 
10263:             � After the ERR bit is set, all of the register bits except the TREF, THIT, and
10264:                   LOST bits (<7:5>) are frozen until software clears the ERR bit.
10265: 
10266:             � If the ERR bit is set, and another IOC error is detected, the LOST bit is
10267:                   set. Because the ERR bit is set, information associated with the second
10268:                   error cannot be logged and is lost. The LOST bit remains set until it is
10269:                   cleared by software.
10270: 
10271:             The IOC_STAT0 register is accessed at address 18000004016. All bits of this
10272:             register are UNDEFINED after reset.
