10777: 6.4.14 Initialization Requirements
10778: 
10779:             After the system power is turned on or after a reset condition (reset_in_l is
10780:             asserted), serial ROM (SROM) code must initialize the IOC registers.
10781: 
10782:             The SROM code does the following:
10783: 
10784:             1. Deasserts the rst_l signal by writing zero (0) to the IOC_SFT_RST register
10785:                   (Section 6.4.7).
10786: 
10787: 6-50 I/O Controller
10788:             2. Clears the ERR and LOST bits by writing ones (1's) to IOC_STAT0 register
10789:                   bits <5:4> (Section 6.4.3).
10790: 
10791:             3. Prevents the IOC from responding to itself by writing zero to the
10792:                   IOC_W_BASE1 and IOC_W_BASE0 registers (Section 6.4.9).
10793: 
10794:             4. Initializes the HAE<31:27> field in the IOC_HAE register (Section 6.4.1).
10795: 
10796:             This level of initialization is sufficient to allow CPU-initiated PCI transfers to
10797:             operate correctly. Boot code must do additional initialization to configure the
10798:             IOC such that it can respond to PCI-initiated transfers (DMA).
10799: 
10800: 6.5 I/O Controller Signal Pins
10801: 
10802:             Sections 6.5.1 through 6.5.16 describe the IOC signal pins.
10803: 
10804: 6.5.1 req_l
10805: 
10806:             The req_l signal is asserted when the CPU needs to initiate a PCI transfer.
10807:             External arbitration logic is required.
10808: 
10809:             The req_l signal is an output-only signal and can be tristated.
10810: 
10811: 6.5.2 gnt_l
10812: 
10813:             The gnt_l signal is asserted by external arbitration logic when the CPU is
10814:             granted ownership of the PCI bus. Digital recommends that the arbiter default
10815:             grant (park) the PCI bus to the CPU when no other device is requesting
10816:             ownership.
10817: 
10818:             During configuration cycles (read or write operations), the IOC performs
10819:             address stepping (drives address and command for two PCI cycles). If the
10820:             gnt_l signal is deasserted after the IOC has driven the address and command
10821:             for one cycle but before the frame_l signal is asserted, the IOC will relinquish
10822:             the bus and wait for the gnt_l signal to be asserted and the PCI bus idle
10823:             condition.
10824: 
10825:                                                                  Note
10826: 
10827:                   The microprocessor might never be able to complete a configuration
10828:                   cycle if the minimum assertion time for the gnt_l signal is one
10829:                   PCI cycle. The system designer must design around this potential
10830:                   problem by giving the microprocessor adequate time to complete its

codex
The manual confirms the mask field, zero-initialization requirement, and ignored reserved-bit writes. It also adds a missing premise: these configuration fields are **write-only**, so readback would preserve the emulator’s existing convention, not prove hardware fidelity. In the fork, the window and TLB registers are stored but never used for translation; `IOC_CONF` alone has a consumer, and it uses only bit 0.
