9200: 
9201: 6.2.9 Configuration Cycles
9202: 
9203:             The PCI architecture specifies a configuration address space for defining
9204:             configuration registers that are used to initialize and configure devices.
9205:             The IOC supports transfers to the configuration address space to access
9206:             the configuration registers. This region supports the same access types and
9207:             masked address generation as sparse space (Section 6.2.6), with the following
9208:             exceptions:
9209: 
9210:             � Configuration space is accessed with CPU address bits a<33:32> = 01 and
9211:                   a<31:29> = 111.
9212: 
9213:             � PCI address bits ad<31:27> = 00000 and the IOC_HAE register is not
9214:                   used.
9215: 
9216:             � PCI address bits ad<1:0> come directly from configuration cycle type
9217:                   register (IOC_CONF, Section 6.4.2) bits <1:0> during CPU-initiated PCI
9218:                   transfers to configuration space.
9219: 
9220:                                                                                                                I/O Controller 6-15
9221:             � A configuration space read or write command (Table 6-2) is issued on the
9222:                   c_be_l<3:0> pins coincident with a read or write operation to this region.
9223: 
9224:             During configuration cycles, addresses are restricted both by the encoding
9225:             requirements of PCI configuration cycles (as described in the PCI Local Bus
9226:             Specification, Revision 2.0) and by the system-dependent implementation of
9227:             PCI initialization device select (IDSEL) encoding. Configuration cycles use one
9228:             cycle of address stepping; that is, the address and command are driven for two
9229:             consecutive cycles.
9230: 
9231: 6.2.10 Special Cycles and Interrupt Acknowledge Cycles
9232: 
9233:             The PCI special cycle command implements a simple broadcast mech-
9234:             anism that allows the broadcast of processor status information and
9235:             sideband signaling. The command is not addressed to a specific device,
9560: 
9561: 6.3.2 PCI Address Translation
9562: 
9563:             Because the PCI uses a 32-bit address and the CPU uses a 34-bit address,
9564:             PCI addresses to which the IOC responds must be translated to an equivalent
9565:             address in the CPU address space. The IOC implements two programmable
9566:             address windows, called PCI target windows, that control PCI peripheral access
9567:             to system memory. A set of three IOC registers is associated with each PCI
9568:             target window: the window base; window mask; and translated base registers
9569:             (IOC_W_BASE<1:0>, Section 6.4.9; IOC_W_MASK<1:0>, Section 6.4.10; and
9570:             IOC_T_BASE<1:0>, Section 6.4.11).
9571: 
9572:             The window mask register IOC_W_MASK provides a mask corresponding
9573:             to bits <31:20> of an incoming PCI address. The size of each window is
9574:             programmed to be from 1 MB to 4 GB by masking bits of the incoming PCI
9575:             address with the IOC_W_MASK register.
9576: 
9577:             Table 6-6 shows the supported values of IOC_W_MASK register bits <31:20>;
9578:             other values are unsupported.
9579: 
9580:                                                    I/O Controller 6-23
9581: Table 6-6 PCI Window Mask
9582: 
9583: IOC_W_MASK           Window
9584:         <31:20>         Size
9585: 
9586: 0000 0000 0000          1 MB
9587: 0000 0000 0001          2 MB
9588: 0000 0000 0011          4 MB
9589: 0000 0000 0111          8 MB
9590: 0000 0000 1111        16 MB
9591: 0000 0001 1111        32 MB
9592: 0000 0011 1111        64 MB
9593: 0000 0111 1111       128 MB
9594: 0000 1111 1111       256 MB
9595: 0001 1111 1111       512 MB
9596: 0011 1111 1111          1 GB
9597: 0111 1111 1111          2 GB
9598: 1111 1111 1111          4 GB
9599: 
9600: IOC_W_BASE register bits <31:20> specify the target window starting address
10410: 
10411: 6.4.5 Translation Buffer Invalidate All Register
10412: 
10413:             A write operation to the translation buffer invalidate all (IOC_TBIA) register
10414:             invalidates all entries in the scatter-gather map TLB at the start of the next
10415:             PCI-initiated transaction (Section 6.3.3).
10416: 
10417:             The IOC_TBIA register is accessed at address 18000008016. All bits of this
10418:             register are reserved and are ignored on write operations and UNDEFINED on
10419:             read operations.
10420: 
10421: 6-42 I/O Controller
10422: 6.4.6 Translation Buffer Enable Register
10423: 
10424:             The translation buffer enable (IOC_TB_ENA) register determines whether the
10425:             scatter-gather map TLB is enabled (Section 6.3.3).
10426: 
10427:             The IOC_TB_ENA register is accessed at address 1800000A0. All bits of this
10428:             register are UNDEFINED after reset.
10429: 
10430:             Figure 6-6 shows the IOC_TB_ENA register format, and Table 6-13 describes
10431:             its fields.
10432: 
10433: Figure 6-6 IOC_TB_ENA Register Format             876              0
10434: 
10435:  63                                               T
10436:                                                   E RES
10437:                                             RES   N
10438: 
10439: Table 6-13 IOC_TB_ENA Register Field Description
10440: 
10441: Bits Field  Type Description
10442: 
10443: 63:8 RES    X   Reserved.
10444: 
10445: 7    TEN    WO  TLB enable--When written with a zero, this bit disables
10446: 
10447:                 the scatter-gather map TLB. The TLB remains disabled
10448: 
10449:                 until this bit is written with a one. Disabling the TLB
10450: 
10451:                 does not disable scatter-gather map translations.
10452: 
10453: 6:0  RES    X   Reserved.
10454: 
10455: 6.4.7 PCI Soft Reset Register
10456: 
10457:             The PCI soft reset (IOC_SFT_RST) register allows software to assert and
10458:             deassert the PCI reset signal rst_l. The required time that the rst_l signal is
10459:             asserted is system dependent and must be timed by software.
10460: 
10461:             The IOC_SFT_RST register is accessed at address 1800000C0. The RST bit
10462:             (<6>) will be set after reset.
10463: 
10464:             Figure 6-7 shows the IOC_SFT_RST register format, and Table 6-14 describes
10465:             its fields.
10530: 
10531: 4:0  RES    X   Reserved.
10532: 
10533: 6.4.9 Window Base Registers
10534: 
10535:             There is one window base (IOC_W_BASE) register for each PCI target
10536:             window. These registers (IOC_W_BASE1, IOC_W_BASE0) specify the starting
10537:             addresses of the PCI target windows in PCI memory address space. The
10538:             window base addresses must be on a naturally aligned address boundary
10539:             equal to the window's size. Additionally, to ensure that only one PCI target
10540:             window can match an incoming PCI address, the PCI target windows must be
10541:             programmed so that they do not respond to overlapping PCI address ranges.
10542:             (See Section 6.3.2 for more information about using these registers.)
10543: 
10544:             Software should ensure that the PCI is idle before updating these registers.
10545: 
10546:             The IOC_W_BASE0 register is accessed at address 18000010016 and the
10547:             IOC_W_BASE1 register is accessed at address 18000012016. All bits of these
10548:             registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
10549: 
10550:             Figure 6-9 shows the IOC_W_BASE register format, and Table 6-16 describes
10551:             its fields.
10552: 
10553:                                                    I/O Controller 6-45
10554: Figure 6-9 IOC_W_BASE1-0 Registers Format
10555: 
10556: 63                            34 33 32 31             20 19       0
10557: 
10558:                      RES      W  S          W_BASE           RES
10559:                               E  G           <31:20>
10560:                               N
10561: 
