src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:707: 		    already served them.  A guest ld.bu or st.b at any of them was a host
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:708: 		    kill (rung-3 witness).  Now: a READ keeps the served byte (the array's
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:709: 		    current byte, said so -- inside a running COUNT word that is the
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:710: 		    tick's value, not a default); a WRITE is DECLINED.  Not a
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:711: 		    backed store: the cased siblings contradict one (SCCERR clears on
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:712: 		    write, the ICRs mask and reassert, PSCALECNT/SPEED/the IACKs are
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:713: 		    read-only), no inspected OpenBSD driver path reaches them (if_ie never
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:714: 		    attaches: unreadable sits at its 82596 address), and a store from the
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:715: 		    one arm 43 offsets reach would add a bounded-write surface.  One
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:716: 		    latched fatal() per offset per instance, the house `(once)' shape --
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:717: 		    unlike PSCALEADJ's UNLATCHED print above (pcc2pscaleflood).  The
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:718: 		    IACK offsets 0x23/0x25 are declined like the rest: modelling them (on
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:719: 		    the SCCRXIACK shape) would open two new entries into the C040 path,
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:720: 		    so pcc2c040kill goes first.  The %= fold above IS the real part's:
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:721: 		    Motorola VMESBCP2 Table 6-1 lists $FFF42040-$FFF42FFF as repeated
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:722: 		    PCCchip2 registers.  */
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:723: 		if (!(d->warned_unimpl & (1ULL << relative_addr))) {
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:724: 			d->warned_unimpl |= 1ULL << relative_addr;
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:725: 			if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:726: 				fatal("[ pcc2: unimplemented write to offset "
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:727: 				    "0x%x (len %d): 0x%x -- declined.  (once) ]\n",
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:728: 				    (int) relative_addr, (int) len, (int) idata);
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:729: 			else
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:730: 				/*  data[0] is the byte actually SERVED; a reload of the
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:731: 				    array could differ: on the end-span path (zero-filled,
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:732: 				    the array byte kept) and inside a running COUNT word,
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:733: 				    whose SIGALRM-driven tick (timer.c) can land between
src\devices\dev_pcc2.c:734: 				    the copy and this line.  A wide read is labelled.  */
